---
import MarketingPage from '../layouts/MarketingPage.astro';

const description = 'Evaluate Shiba as an open-source Devin alternative: try real company work, review the result, and understand the self-hosting trade-off.';
const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: 'Open-Source Devin Alternative: A Practical Evaluation Guide', description,
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Shiba', url: 'https://tryshiba.dev' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Shiba', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://tryshiba.dev/assets/mascot/shiba-logo-512.png' } },
  datePublished: '2026-09-26', dateModified: '2026-11-01',
  mainEntityOfPage: 'https://tryshiba.dev/open-source-devin-alternative/', image: 'https://tryshiba.dev/assets/og/shiba-og.png',
};
const questions = [
  ['Useful output', 'Can the employee return something your team can inspect: a code change, brief, report, or checklist?'],
  ['Permission', 'Can you see the proposed request before repository work starts, including whether a pull request will be published?'],
  ['Review', 'Can you read the files and reported checks, spot missing evidence, and decide what to use?'],
  ['Operation', 'Are you willing to set up the installation, manage access, and pay the hosting and model providers?'],
];
---

<MarketingPage
  title="Open-Source Devin Alternative: A Practical Guide — Shiba"
  description={description}
  path="/open-source-devin-alternative/"
  type="article"
  publishedTime="2026-09-26T00:00:00Z"
  modifiedTime="2026-11-01T00:00:00Z"
  schema={articleSchema}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Open-Source Devin Alternative', path: '/open-source-devin-alternative/' }]}
>
  <section class="shell hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">An evaluation guide</p>
    <h1>Looking for an open-source<br /><em>Devin alternative?</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">Start with the work you need done. Shiba gives solo builders and teams a self-hosted workspace for AI employees across engineering, design, marketing, sales, operations, finance, and research.</p>
    <p class="intro-note">We build Shiba. This guide is a way to evaluate it, not a claim that it matches every Devin feature or performs better.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button" href="/docs/getting-started/">Try a small task <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a class="button button-outline" href="https://github.com/opentoolsorg/shiba" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="shell guide">
    <section aria-labelledby="comparison-matrix-title">
      <h2 id="comparison-matrix-title">What you choose with Shiba</h2>
      <p>The software is open source under AGPL-3.0-only. You run it in your own Cloudflare account, choose a configured model, and manage access to the workspace.</p>
      <p>That gives you control and responsibility. Hosting and model usage cost extra, and someone needs to maintain the installation. Shiba is under development; review the <a href="/docs/readiness/">readiness checklist</a> before relying on a live deployment.</p>
      <p>For any hosted alternative, check the provider's current product and pricing information against your requirements. We have not run a head-to-head benchmark or verified comparative cost savings.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="priorities-title">
      <h2 id="priorities-title">Use four questions to judge the fit.</h2>
      <dl class="question-list">
        {questions.map(([label, question]) => <div><dt>{label}</dt><dd>{question}</dd></div>)}
      </dl>
      <p>Employees describe responsibilities, not separate models. The built-in templates are Engineering, Marketing, Research, and Operations; other roles use custom instructions.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="bounded-title">
      <h2 id="bounded-title">Try one task you can check.</h2>
      <p>Choose a low-risk example from your own work. Give the employee the relevant context and say what should come back.</p>
      <ul class="examples">
        <li><strong>Engineering:</strong> fix a reproducible bug and add a regression test.</li>
        <li><strong>Marketing or design:</strong> turn product notes into a launch brief or a design specification.</li>
        <li><strong>Sales or revenue:</strong> draft an account brief or summarize supplied pipeline notes.</li>
        <li><strong>Operations or finance:</strong> write a handoff checklist or draft a budget from figures you provide.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Every execution currently needs a GitHub repository, including non-code tasks. Documents are drafts for your review. A role does not connect an account, update a CRM, send outreach, run bookkeeping, or authorize payments.</p>
      <ol class="pilot-steps">
        <li>Describe the task, the repository, and the expected output.</li>
        <li>Read the proposed request and approve standard repository execution only when it matches your intent.</li>
        <li>Inspect the files, changes, and checks. Note what was missing or needed correction.</li>
        <li>Compare the setup effort, review time, and actual hosting and model charges with your other options.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="cost-title">
      <h2 id="cost-title">Free software. Separate running costs.</h2>
      <p>You do not need a Shiba subscription or an invitation to self-host the source. You pay the hosting and model providers you configure. Your task size, model, and usage determine those costs.</p>
      <p>See <a href="/docs/costs/">Costs</a> and <a href="/docs/self-hosting/">Self-hosting</a> before setting up an installation. Keep publication off for the first task, then review the result before deciding what to share.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="closing-section" aria-labelledby="next-title">
      <h2 id="next-title">Evaluate the work, not the promise.</h2>
      <p>A small task will tell you more about the fit than a feature checklist. Start there, and keep the final decision with your team.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button" href="/docs/getting-started/">Read the quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="button button-outline" href="/why-shiba/">Why I built Shiba</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</MarketingPage>

<style>
  .hero { padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 104px); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 4.5rem); max-width: 1000px; }
  .hero .lead { max-width: 68ch; }
  .intro-note { max-width: 66ch; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .hero-actions .button { min-height: 44px; }
  .guide { max-width: 1000px; }
  .guide > section { padding-block: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .guide h2 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.2vw, 2.8rem); text-wrap: balance; }
  .guide p { max-width: 70ch; color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.75; }
  .question-list { margin-block: 28px; }
  .question-list > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 140px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 24px; padding-block: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .question-list dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); }
  .question-list dd { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.65; }
  .examples, .pilot-steps { max-width: 70ch; padding-left: 1.3rem; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .examples li, .pilot-steps li { margin-block: 14px; line-height: 1.65; }
  .examples strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .closing-section { border-bottom: 0 !important; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .question-list > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; } .hero-actions .button { width: 100%; } }
</style>
